{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call_d7eYCqp10HudpI0rCP75o22T\nfc_036eba6715c5cf21016aadb880fd1c87d198983b3be7931847","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/psudokit/.claude/skills/debugging/SKILL.md"},"result":{"success":{"content":"---\nname: debugging\ndescription: >\n  Systematically find the root cause of a bug instead of guessing at fixes. Use when the user\n  says \"debug this\", \"why is this failing\", \"find the root cause\", \"this isn't working\",\n  \"track down the bug\", pastes an error/stack trace, or describes broken behavior. Enforces\n  reproduce → isolate → hypothesize → verify before proposing any fix.\n---\n\n# Debugging (root-cause first)\n\nCheap fixes that treat symptoms create new bugs. This skill drives to the actual cause.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Reproduce.** Get a reliable repro (exact steps, inputs, environment). If it can't be\n   reproduced, that's the first problem to solve — add logging/instrumentation.\n2. **Read the error literally.** Full stack trace, top frame in *your* code, exact message.\n   Don't skim — the answer is often in the line you skipped.\n3. **Isolate.** Narrow the surface: bisect (git bisect / comment-out), binary-search the input,\n   or add assertions to find where reality diverges from expectation.\n4. **Hypothesize one cause** and state what you'd expect to see if it's true.\n5. **Verify** with evidence — a log line, a test, a debugger value — before claiming it's the cause.\n   Never assert a fix works without observing the corrected behavior.\n6. **Fix the cause, not the symptom.** Then add a regression test that fails before / passes after.\n\n## Techniques\n\n- **Print/log strategically** — log inputs and outputs at boundaries, not everywhere.\n- **git bisect** — when it \"used to work\", find the exact commit that broke it.\n- **Rubber-duck the assumptions** — list what you *believe* is true; check each one.\n- **Minimal repro** — strip the failing case to the smallest program that still fails.\n\n## Rules\n\n- One hypothesis at a time. Changing five things at once means you learn nothing.\n- If a \"fix\" works but you don't know *why*, you're not done — you got lucky.\n- Hand off to **verification-before-completion** before claiming the bug is fixed.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":39,"fileSize":1990,"path":"/Users/psudokit/.claude/skills/debugging/SKILL.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":39},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call_d7eYCqp10HudpI0rCP75o22T\nfc_036eba6715c5cf21016aadb880fd1c87d198983b3be7931847","startedAtMs":"1789769857094","completedAtMs":"1789769858534"},"model_call_id":"0fa16de5-695b-4488-8fe5-b77b920f4b3f-0-dxlk","session_id":"1643c25c-f607-4100-8e10-c70b37e591a0","timestamp_ms":1789769858672}
